.TH CMAP 2 "PDP-11 Only"
.SH NAME
cmap \- remap the code segment of a program
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B cmap
is used to remap a different portion of code into a process' address
space.
This call is used by a process which is too big to fit into 64kb of
address space.
.SH "SEE ALSO"
``Code-Mapping Under VENIX'' in the
.I "Programming Guide"
.br
ld(1), sdata(2)
.SH NOTES
Code-mapping is not portable to standard UNIX.
This call should not
be used directly by the user; the loader is set up to deal with code-mapping
when given the
.B \-m
flag.
.SH ASSEMBLER
(cmap = 62.)
.TP
PDP-11:
.nf
R0 = offset
sys cmap
R0 = \-1 if error, 0 if okay
.fi
.sp
